attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on the `glp` genes.** Columns 0 to 5, `glpD` to `rtcB`, are carried by 92 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 2% of calls {S1}. The model names 93 to 99% of them, fewest at column 4, `rtcR`, 93% {S1}.

@variable **A variable column follows at `rtcA`**, column 6, carried by 90% {S2.c6}. Then columns 7 to 13, `malT` to `bioH`, are [[maltodextrin metabolism]], carried by 95 to 97% {S3, Q}. Columns 15 to 17, `feoC` to `feoA`, are [[ferrous iron transport]] {S5, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 95%, and hesitates less there, 0.09 against 0.18 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 0, `glpD`, is a spine column, at 0.50 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on a fork column.** Column 79, `yheO`, is carried by 88% of chromosomes, with `tusD` at 57% {S10, E}. The last column is `yheO` {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 97% of genes**, 0.10 bits on average, perplexity 1.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.22 against 0.09 bits, and names about as many genes, 95% against 98% {C}.

